### Change View() Return Type from string to tea.View

Source: https://github.com/charmbracelet/bubbletea/blob/v2.0.0/UPGRADE_GUIDE_V2.md

In Bubble Tea v2, the View() method now returns a `tea.View` struct instead of a string. This allows for more declarative control over the UI.

```go
// Before:
func (m model) View() string {
    return "Hello, world!"
}

// After:
func (m model) View() tea.View {
    return tea.NewView("Hello, world!")
}
```

```go
func (m model) View() tea.View {
    var v tea.View
    v.SetContent("Hello, world!")
    v.AltScreen = true
    return v
}
```

--------------------------------

### Migrate Bubble Tea Application from v1 to v2

Source: https://github.com/charmbracelet/bubbletea/blob/v2.0.0/UPGRADE_GUIDE_V2.md

A side-by-side comparison showing the shift from v1 program-level configuration to v2's view-based configuration. It demonstrates updated message types, the new View return type, and simplified program initialization.

```go
// v1
package main

import (
    "fmt"
    "os"

